[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71022,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Basal cell carcinoma of the scrotum (BCC-S) is a carcinoma derived from basal cells of the interfollicular epidermis and/or hair follicle, histologically similar to carcinomas found in sun-exposed areas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71023,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8090/3 Basal cell carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71024,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C81.Y &amp; XH2615 Other specified malignant neoplasm of penis &amp; Basal cell carcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71025,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71026,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Potentially all subtypes of basal cell carcinoma (BCC) of sun-exposed skin can be found, although the majority of cases reported are of the nodular and superficial types.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71027,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Scrotum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71028,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Isolated case reports constitute the basis of knowledge about BCC-S, with patients ranging in age from 42&nbsp;to 82&nbsp;years {10439525; 20877361}. BCC-S typically appears as red papules, plaques, or nodules, and local invasion is the rule {22309181}. There are no specific symptoms, and in most cases diagnosis is delayed for several years {22309181}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71029,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>BCCs involving the genital epithelium are rare, with an incidence of &lt;&nbsp;0.1&nbsp;cases per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;person-years {20877361; 33102034}. They account for 5&ndash;19% of all scrotal tumours {18799208}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71030,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. An association with lichen simplex chronicus and other inflammatory conditions has been suggested {7057490}. Studies have failed to demonstrate an association with HPV {15663663}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71031,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although mutations in <em>TP53</em> and <em>PTCH1</em> are associated with sun-exposed sporadic BCC, there have been no molecular studies of BCC-S. Both mutations are associated with ultraviolet (UV) exposure and are not known to be associated with BCC-S {32759706}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71032,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumour size varies from 10&nbsp;to 50&nbsp;mm {22309181}, with no specific gross appearances.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71033,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histologically, the lesions are similar to BCCs of other sites. The proliferating nests and cords of basaloid cells show the characteristic peripheral palisading with occasional central squamous differentiation, microcyst formation, and retraction spaces.</p>\r\n<p>BCC should be distinguished from basaloid carcinoma, an aggressive subtype of squamous cell carcinoma. Basaloid carcinoma is characterized by a typical downward proliferation of nests composed of small anaplastic cells with numerous mitoses and often with central necrosis {21167410}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71034,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71035,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71036,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> basaloid epithelium typically forms a palisade with a cleft forming from the adjacent tumour stroma; crowded nuclei with scattered mitotic figures; mucinous stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71037,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging system for scrotal cancer was proposed by Lowe and is not included in the current American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging classification {1574830; 29325693}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71038,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 312,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The treatment of choice is surgery. Because of the difficulty of defining the edges of the tumour, Mohs microscopic surgery has been suggested as the best option {33102034}. BCC-S has been reported to be more aggressive and more likely to metastasize than BCC arising at other sites {22309181}. Therefore, patients with BCC-S should be kept under surveillance for metastasis for 2&ndash;5&nbsp;years after excision of the tumour {29377295}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:58:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]